{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "EZK",
  "chapter": 21,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the word of the LORD came to me, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Son of man, set thy face towards Jerusalem, and drop ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy word",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " towards the holy places, and prophesy against the land of Israel,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And say to the land of Israel, Thus saith the LORD; Behold, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against thee, and will draw forth my sword out of its sheath, and will cut off from thee the righteous and the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seeing then that I will cut off from thee the righteous and the wicked, therefore shall my sword go forth from its sheath against all flesh from the south to the north:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That all flesh may know that I the LORD have drawn my sword out of its sheath: it shall not return any more.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sigh therefore, thou son of man, with the breaking of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " loins; and with bitterness sigh before their eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it shall be, when they say to thee, Why sighest thou? that thou shalt answer, For the tidings; because it cometh: and every heart shall melt, and all hands shall be feeble, and every spirit shall faint, and all knees shall be weak ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " water: behold, it cometh, and shall be brought to pass, saith the Lord GOD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Again the word of the LORD came to me, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Son of man, prophesy, and say, Thus saith the LORD; Say, A sword, a sword is sharpened, and also furbished:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is sharpened to make a grievous slaughter; it is furbished that it may glitter: should we then make mirth? it contemneth the rod of my son, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " every tree.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he hath given it to be furbished, that it may be handled: the sword is sharpened, and it is furbished, to give it into the hand of the slayer.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Cry and howl, son of man: for it shall be upon my people, it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon all the princes of Israel: terrors by reason of the sword shall be upon my people: smite therefore upon ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thigh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a trial, and what if ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the sword",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " contemneth even the rod? it shall be no ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "more",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", saith the Lord GOD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou therefore, son of man, prophesy, and smite ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hands together, and let the sword be doubled the third time, the sword of the slain: it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the sword of the great ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " slain, which entereth into their private chambers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have set the point of the sword against all their gates, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " heart may faint, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ruins be multiplied: ah! ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " made bright, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sharpened for the slaughter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Go thee one way or other, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "either",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on the right hand, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on the left, whithersoever thy face ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " set.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will also smite my hands together, and I will cause my fury to rest: I the LORD have said ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The word of the LORD came to me again, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also, thou son of man, appoint thee two ways, that the sword of the king of Babylon may come: both ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "ways",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shall come forth from one land: and choose thou a place, choose ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at the head of the way to the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Appoint a way, that the sword may come to Rabbah of the Ammonites, and to Judah in Jerusalem the fortified.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the king of Babylon stood at the parting of the way, at the head of the two ways, to use divination; he made ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " arrows bright, he consulted with images, he looked in the liver.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At his right hand was the divination for Jerusalem, to appoint captains, to open the mouth in the slaughter, to lift up the voice with shouting, to appoint ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "battering",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rams against the gates, to cast a mount, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to build a fort.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it shall be to them as a false divination in their sight, to them that have sworn oaths: but he will call to remembrance the iniquity, that they may be taken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; Because ye have made your iniquity to be remembered, in that your transgressions are disclosed, so that in all your doings your sins do appear; because, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I say",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", that ye are come to remembrance, ye shall be taken with the hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou, profane wicked prince of Israel, whose day is come, when iniquity ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an end,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the Lord GOD; Remove the diadem, and take off the crown: this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the same: exalt ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " low, and abase ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " high.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will overturn, overturn, overturn it: and it shall be no ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "more",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", until he cometh whose right it is; and I will give it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou, son of man, prophesy and say, Thus saith the Lord GOD concerning the Ammonites, and concerning their reproach; even say thou, The sword, the sword ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " drawn: for the slaughter ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " furbished, to consume because of the glittering:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "While they see vanity to thee, while they divine a lie to thee, to bring thee upon the necks of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " slain, of the wicked, whose day is come, when their iniquity ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an end.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall I cause ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to return into its sheath? I will judge thee in the place where thou wast created, in the land of thy nativity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will pour out my indignation upon thee, I will blow against thee in the fire of my wrath, and deliver thee into the hand of brutish men, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " skillful to destroy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.21.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.21.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt be for fuel to the fire; thy blood shall be in the midst of the land; thou shalt be no ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "more",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " remembered: for I the LORD have spoken ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
